{
  "title": "58: al-Mujaadelah المجادلة",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nقَدْ سَمِعَ اللّٰهُ قَوْلَ الَّتِىْ تُجَادِلُكَ فِىْ زَوْجِهَا وَ تَشْتَكِىْۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ ۖ وَاللّٰهُ يَسْمَعُ تَحَاوُرَكُمَا ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ سَمِيْعٌ ۢ بَصِيْرٌ‏(1)\nQAD SAMEA’A LAAHO QAWLA LATEE TUJAADELUKA FEE ZAWJEHAA WA TASHTAKEAA ELAL LAAHE WAL LAAHO YASMA-O’ TAHAAWURAKUMAA INNAL LAAHA SAMEE-U’N BASEER.\nIndeed, hath God heard the statement of her who pleadeth with thee about her husband and petitioneth unto God; and verily God heareth the contention of you two; Verily God is All-Hearing, All-Seeing.\nاَلَّذِيْنَ يُظٰهِرُوْنَ مِنْكُمْ مِّنْ نِّسَآئِهِمْ مَّا هُنَّ اُمَّهٰتِهِمْؕ اِنْ اُمَّهٰتُهُمْ اِلَّا الّٰٓىِئْ وَلَدْنَهُمْؕ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مُنْكَرًا مِّنَ الْقَوْلِ وَزُوْرًاؕ وَ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَعَفُوٌّ غَفُوْرٌ‏(2)\nLAZEENA YUZAAHEROONA MINKUM MIN NESAAA-EHIM MAA HUNNA AUMMAHAATEHEM IN AUMMAHAATUHUM ILLAA ALLAAA WALADNAHUM WA INNAHUM LAYAQOOLOONA MUNKARAN MENAL AL-QAWLE WAZOORAN WA INNAL LAAHA LAA’AFOO GHAFOORUR.\nThose of you who abandon any of their wives through ‘Zihar’ (by saying “Be thou unto me as my mother’s back”); they are not their mothers; their mothers are only those who gave them birth! and certainly they utter a word hateful and false; and verily God is Pardoning, Oft-Forgiving.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُظٰهِرُوْنَ مِنْ نِّسَآئِهِمْ ثُمَّ يَعُوْدُوْنَ لِمَا قَالُوْا فَتَحْرِيْرُ رَقَبَةٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّتَمَآسَّا ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ تُوْعَظُوْنَ بِهٖ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(3)\nWAL LAZEENA YUZAAHEROONA MIN NESAAA-EHIM SUMMA YAU’OODOONA LEMAKH QAALOO FATAHREERU RAQABATIN MIN QABLE AN YYATAMAASSAA ZAA ZAALEKUM TOOA’AZOONA BEHI WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOON KHABEERUM.\nAnd those who abandon any of their wives through ‘Zihar’ and then would recall what they have uttered, they may free a captive ere they touch each other; that ye are admonished (to conform); and Verily God, of whatever ye do, is Well-Aware.\nفَمَنْ لَّمْ يَجِدْ فَصِيَامُ شَهْرَيْنِ مُتَتَابِعَيْنِ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يَّتَمَآسَّاؕ فَمَنْ لَّمْ يَسْتَطِعْ فَاِطْعَامُ سِتِّيْنَ مِسْكِيْنًاؕ ذٰلِكَ لِتُؤْمِنُوْا بِاللّٰهِ وَرَسُوْلِهٖؕ وَتِلْكَ حُدُوْدُ اللّٰهِؕ وَلِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابٌ اَلِیْمٌ‏(4)\nFAMAN LAM YAJID FA-SEYAAMO SHAHRAYNE MUTATAABEA’AYNE MIN QABLE AN YYATAMAASSAA FAMAN LAM YASTATEA’ FAATA’AAMU SETTEENA MESKEENAN ZAALEKA LE-LAM TOAMENOO BIL-LAAHE WARASOOLEH WA TILKAL TILKA LAAH WA LIL KAAFEREENA A’ZAABUN AALEMUN.\nBut whosoever findeth not the means (to free a captive), he may fast for two months consecutively ere they touch each other; and whosoever is not able to do (so) shall feed sixty needy ones; that is in order that ye may believe in God and His Apostle; And these are the bounds set of God; And for the disbeliever there shall be a painful chastisement.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُحَآدُّوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ كُبِتُوْا كَمَا كُبِتَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ وَقَدْ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اٰيٰتٍۢ بَيِّنٰتٍ ؕ وَ لِلْكٰفِرِيْنَ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ ۚ‏(5)\nINNAL LAZEENA YUHAADDOONA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU KUBETOOA KAMAA KUBETA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM WA QAD ANZALNAA AAYAATIM BAYYENAAT WA LIL KAAFEREENA A’ZAABUN MOHEEN.\nVerily, those who oppose God and His Apostle, shall be humiliated as were humiliated those before them; and indeed We have sent down signs clear; and for the disbelievers there shall be a humiliating chastisement.\nيَوْمَ يَبْعَثُهُمُ اللّٰهُ جَمِيْعًا فَيُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا عَمِلُوْا ؕ اَحْصٰٮهُ اللّٰهُ وَنَسُوْهُ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدٌ‏(6)\nYAWMA YABA’ASUHUMU LAAHO JAMEE-A’A FAYUNABBEUHUM BEMAA A’MELOO AAHSAAHU LAAHO WANASOOHU WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN WA.\nOn the day when God will raise them all to life and inform them of what they did; God hath encompassed (everything) in (His) record; while they (might) have forgotten it; and God is over all things a Witness.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اَنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِؕ مَا يَكُوْنُ مِنْ نَّجْوٰى ثَلٰثَةٍ اِلَّا هُوَ رَابِعُهُمْ وَلَا خَمْسَةٍ اِلَّا هُوَ سَادِسُهُمْ وَلَاۤ اَدْنٰى مِنْ ذٰ لِكَ وَلَاۤ اَكْثَرَ اِلَّا هُوَ مَعَهُمْ اَيْنَ مَا كَانُوْاۚ ثُمَّ يُنَبِّئُهُمْ بِمَا عَمِلُوْا يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(7)\nALAM TARA ANNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZ MAA LAHUL MIN NNAJWAA SALAASATIN ILLAA HOWA RAABEU’UHUM WA LAA KHAMSATIN ILLAA HOWA SAADESUHUM WA LAA ADNAA MIN ZAA LEKA WA LAA AKSARAN ILLAA HOWA MA-A’HUM AYNA MAA KAANOO SUMMA YUNABBEUHUM BEMAA A’MELOO YAWMA QEYAAMATE INNAL LAAHA BEKULLE SHAY-IN A’LEEM.\nSeest thou not that God knoweth whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth? nowhere taketh place any secret counsel between three (persons) but He is fourth of them, nor between five, but He is the sixth, nor (between) less than that, nor (between) more but He is with them wheresoever they may be; then will He inform them of whatever they did, on the Day of Judgment - Verily God Well Knoweth all things.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ نُهُوْا عَنِ النَّجْوٰى ثُمَّ يَعُوْدُوْنَ لِمَا نُهُوْا عَنْهُ وَيَتَنٰجَوْنَ بِالْاِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ وَمَعْصِيَتِ الرَّسُوْلِ وَاِذَا جَآءُوْكَ حَيَّوْكَ بِمَا لَمْ يُحَيِّكَ بِهِ اللّٰهُۙ وَيَقُوْلُوْنَ فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ لَوْلَا يُعَذِّبُنَا اللّٰهُ بِمَا نَقُوْلُؕ حَسْبُهُمْ جَهَنَّمُۚ يَصْلَوْنَهَاۚ فَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(8)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA NUHOOA A’NIL AN-NAJWAA SUMMA YAU’OODOONA LEMAKH NUHOOA A’NHO WAYATANAAJAWNA BIL-ISME WAL U’UDWAANE WAMAA’SEETE RASOOLE WA EZAA JAAOOKA HAYWKA BEMAA LAM YUHAYKA BEHIL LAAHO WA YAQOOLOONA FEE ANFOSEHIM LAWLAA YUA’AZZEBUNAA LAAHO BEMAA NAQOOLU HASBUHUM JAHANNAMUL YASLAWNAHAA FA MASALUL MASEER.\nSeest thou not those who have been forbidden secret counsels, yet return they unto what hath been forbidden and hold they secret counsels to sin and revolt and towards disobedience to the Apostle, and when come they unto thee, they greet thee, not as greeteth thee God; and say they in their selves “Why doth God chastise not for what we say?” Enough for them is hell, they shall enter it, and what a wretched destination it is!\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا تَنَاجَيْتُمْ فَلَا تَتَنَاجَوْا بِالْاِثْمِ وَالْعُدْوَانِ وَمَعْصِيَتِ الرَّسُوْلِ وَتَنَاجَوْا بِالْبِرِّ وَالتَّقْوٰىؕ وَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ الَّذِىْۤ اِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(9)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA TANAAJAYTUM FALAA TATANAAJAWA BIL-ISME WAL U’UDWAANE WAMAA’SEETE RASOOLE WATANAAJAWA BIL-BIRRE WAALTTAQWAA WAT TAQUL LAAHA LAZEE ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\nO’ ye who believe! When ye counsel among yourselves in secret, then counsel ye not to sin and revolt and disobedience to the Apostle, but counsel ye among yourselves for goodness and restrain (of yourselves against evil)’, and fear ye (the wrath of) God unto Whom ye shall all be gathered!\nاِنَّمَا النَّجْوٰى مِنَ الشَّيْطٰنِ لِيَحْزُنَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَلَيْسَ بِضَآرِّهِمْ شَيْئًا اِلَّا بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِؕ وَعَلَى اللّٰهِ فَلْيَتَوَكَّلِ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(10)\nINNAMAA AN-NAJWAA MENAL SHAYTAANE LEEHZUNA LAZEENA AAMANOO BE-AN BEZAARREHEM SHAY-ANW ILLAA BE-IZNIL LAAH WA LAAHE FALYATAWAKKALE MOAMENOONA.\nSecret counsels are (Simulated) only by satan, that he may cause grief unto those who believe, but he shall harm them not in any way but with the permission of God; and upon God alone depend those who believe.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا قِيْلَ لَكُمْ تَفَسَّحُوْا فِى الْمَجٰلِسِ فَافْسَحُوْا يَفْسَحِ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ ۚ وَاِذَا قِيْلَ انْشُزُوْا فَانْشُزُوْا يَرْفَعِ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مِنْكُمْ ۙ وَالَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ دَرَجٰتٍ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(11)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA QEELA LAKUM TAFASSAHOOA FIL AL-MAJAALESE FAAFSAHOOA YAFSAHE LAAHO LAKUM WA EZAA QEELA ANSHUZOOA FAANSHUZOOA YARFAE’E LAAHO LAZEENA AAMANOO MINKUM WAL LAZEENA OOTUL OOTUL I’LMA DARAJAATIN WAL LAAHO BEMAA TA’MALOON KHABEERUM.\nO’ ye who believe! when it is said unto you, ‘Make ye room in (your) assemblies! then make ye room, God will make room for you; and when it is said unto you, ‘Rise ye up! then rise ye up, God will exalt (you in) ranks (unto Him), those who believe among you, and those who have been granted knowledge; and God is All-Aware of whatsoever ye do.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِذَا نَاجَيْتُمُ الرَّسُوْلَ فَقَدِّمُوْا بَيْنَ يَدَىْ نَجْوٰٮكُمْ صَدَقَةً  ؕ ذٰ لِكَ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ وَاَطْهَرُ ؕ فَاِنْ لَّمْ تَجِدُوْا فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(12)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO EZAA NAAJAYTUMU YATTABE-U’R FAQADDEMOOA BAYNA YADAY NAJWAAKUM SADAQATAN ZAA LEKA KHAYRUL LAKUM WA ATHARO FA-IN LAM WA LAM FA-INNAL LAAHA GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nO’ ye who believe! When ye (wish to) consult in private with the Apostle, then offer some alms before your consultation, that is better for you and purer; but ye find not any means (to do so), then verily God is Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\nءَاَشْفَقْتُمْ اَنْ تُقَدِّمُوْا بَيْنَ يَدَىْ نَجْوٰٮكُمْ صَدَقٰتٍ ؕ فَاِذْ لَمْ تَفْعَلُوْا وَتَابَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكُمْ فَاَقِيْمُوا الصَّلٰوةَ وَ اٰتُوا الزَّكٰوةَ وَاَطِيْعُوا اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ خَبِيْرٌۢ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(13)\nAASHFAQTUM AN WA BAYNA YADAY NAJWAAKUM SADAQAATIN FA IZ LAM TAF-A’LOO WA TAABA LAAHO A’LAYKUM FAAQEEMOOA SALAATA WA AAATOOA ZAKAATA WAATEEU’OOA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WAL LAAHO KHABEERUM BEMAA TA’MALOON.\nWhat Restrained ye that ye give alms before your consultation? Then since ye did it not and God turned (merciful) unto you, then keep ye up (the regular) prayer, and pay ye (the prescribed) poor-rate and obey ye God and His Apostle; and God is All-Aware of what (all) ye do.\nاَلَمْ تَرَ اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ تَوَلَّوْا قَوْمًا غَضِبَ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِمْؕ مَّا هُمْ مِّنْكُمْ وَلَا مِنْهُمْۙ وَيَحْلِفُوْنَ عَلَى الْكَذِبِ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(14)\nALAM TARA ELAL LAZEENA TAWALLAW QAWMAN GHAZEBAL LAAHO A’ALAYHEM MAA HUM MINKUM WA LAA MINHUM WAYAHLEFOONA A’LAL AL-KAZEBE WA HUM YA’LAMOON.\nHast thou not seen those who befriend a people on whom hath been the wrath of God? Thy are neither of your party nor are they of theirs, and swear they for falsehood while they know (what they do).\nاَعَدَّ اللّٰهُ لَهُمْ عَذَابًا شَدِيْدًا ؕ اِنَّهُمْ سَآءَ مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(15)\nA-A’DDA LAAHO LAHUM A’ZAABAN SHADEEDAA INNAHUM SAAA-A MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nFor them hath prepared God a severe chastisement; Verily, evil is what they do.\nاِتَّخَذُوْۤا اَيْمَانَهُمْ جُنَّةً فَصَدُّوْا عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ فَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ‏(16)\nITTAKHAZOO AYMAANAHUM JUNNATAN FA-SADDU A’N SABEELIL LAAHE FALAHUM A’ZAABUN MOHEEN.\nMake they their oaths a shield, and obstruct they (others) from the way of God, so for them shall be a shameful chastisement.\nلَنْ تُغْنِىَ عَنْهُمْ اَمْوَالُهُمْ وَلَاۤ اَوْلَادُهُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ النَّارِ ؕ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(17)\nLAN TUGHNEAAA A’NHUM AAMWAALUHUM WA LAA AAWLAADUHUM MENAL LAAHE SHAY-ANW OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN NAAR HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nNever shall avail them aught against God, their wealth nor their children; they are fellows of the fire; they shall abide therein.\nيَوْمَ يَبْعَثُهُمُ اللّٰهُ جَمِيْعًا فَيَحْلِفُوْنَ لَهٗ كَمَا يَحْلِفُوْنَ لَكُمْ وَيَحْسَبُوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ عَلٰى شَىْءٍ ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّهُمْ هُمُ الْكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(18)\nYAWMA YABA’ASUHUMU LAAHO JAMEE-A’A FAYAHLEFOONA LAHU KAMAA YAHLEFOONA LAKUM WA YAHSABOONAL ANNAHUM A’LAA SHAY-IN ALAA INNAHUM HOMUL AL-KAAZEBOONA.\nOn the day when God will raise them all, then will swear they unto Him as they swear unto you, and deem they that it will avail them. Nay! verily they, they are the liars!\nاِسْتَحْوَذَ عَلَيْهِمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ فَاَنْسٰٮهُمْ ذِكْرَ اللّٰهِؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ حِزْبُ الشَّيْطٰنِؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ حِزْبَ الشَّيْطٰنِ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(19)\nAESTAHWAZA A’LAYHEMUL SHAYTAANO FA-ANSAAHUM ZEKRA LAAH OOLAAA-EKA HEZBU SHAYTAAN ALAA INNAL HEZBA SHAYTAANE HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nSatan hath gained hold on them, so he maketh them forget the remembrance of God; They are Satan’s Party; Beware! verily, the party of Satan are the losers.\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ يُحَآدُّوْنَ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗۤ اُولٰٓئِكَ فِى الْاَذَلِّيْنَ‏(20)\nINNAL LAZEENA YUHAADDOONA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU OOLAAA-EKA FIL AL-AAZALLEENA.\nVerily those who are opposed to God, and His Apostle, they shall be of the most humiliated.\nكَتَبَ اللّٰهُ لَاَغْلِبَنَّ اَنَا وَرُسُلِىْؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ قَوِىٌّ عَزِيْزٌ‏(21)\nKATABAL LAAHO LAAGHLEBANNA ANAA WARUSULEAA INNAL LAAHA QAWEAAAUN A’ZEEZUN.\nGod hath decreed: “I shall prevail, I and My apostles!” Verily God is the All-Strong, the Ever-Prevalent.\nلَا تَجِدُ قَوْمًا يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ بِاللّٰهِ وَالْيَوْمِ الْاٰخِرِ يُوَآدُّوْنَ مَنْ حَآدَّ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ وَلَوْ كَانُوْۤا اٰبَآءَهُمْ اَوْ اَبْنَآءَهُمْ اَوْ اِخْوَانَهُمْ اَوْ عَشِيْرَتَهُمْؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ كَتَبَ فِىْ قُلُوْبِهِمُ الْاِيْمَانَ وَاَيَّدَهُمْ بِرُوْحٍ مِّنْهُ ؕ وَيُدْخِلُهُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ؕ رَضِىَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمْ وَرَضُوْا عَنْهُ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ حِزْبُ اللّٰهِ ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ حِزْبَ اللّٰهِ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(22)\nLAA TAJEDU QAWMAN YOAMENOON BIL-LAAHE WAL YAWMIL AAKHERE YOOAAADDOONA MAN HAADDA LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU WA LAW KAANOO AA-BAAA-AHUM AW YOZABBEHO AW AEKHWAANAHUM AW A’ASHEERATAHUM OOLAAA-EKA KATABAL FEE QOLOOBEHEMUR EEMAANA WAAYYADAHUM BEROOHIN MINHO WAYUDKHELUHUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA RAZEYAL LAAHO A’NHUM WARAZOOA A’NHO OOLAAA-EKA HEZBU LAAHE ALAA INNAL HEZBA LAAHE HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nThou shalt find not a people who believe in God and the hereafter befriending those who oppose God and His Apostle, be they even their own fathers, or their sons, or their own brothers, or their kinsmen, they are those God hath inscribed faith in their hearts and hath strengthened them with a Spirit from Himself; and He will admit them into gardens ‘neath which flow rivers, they shall abide therein; with God well pleased with them, and they will be well-pleased with God; They are the party of God; Be it known, verily the party of God alone shall be the successful ones.",
  "merits": "Surah Mujaadelah (The Pleading One)\nThere are 22 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Madinah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the one who recites this Surah will be from among the thankful servants of Allah (s.w.t.) on the Day of Judgement. If Surah al-Mujaadelah is recited near a sick person, or worn by the sick person as a talisman, he will be cured of his illness. If recited on anything that has been buried in the ground, it will remain protected until the person himself removes it.\nReciting this Surah brings a feeling of ease to a restless person. Constant recitation also protects one from thieves. Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that recitation of this Surah keeps one safe from the evil designs of Jinn and men. If recited on dust or sand and then thrown towards the enemy, he is easily overcome."
